WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.100
The news has been rough in the world of Spider-Man.

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:07.200
In the days since it was reported that Disney
and Sony were going their separate ways, unable

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.040
to reach an agreement regarding their joint
partnership over the Spider-Man franchise,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.460
many have been playing the blame game and
firing shots at both studios.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.560
Thanks to a new report from Variety breaking
down the Spider-Man split, we may finally

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.080
know who to point our fingers at.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.189
According to an unnamed source with inside
knowledge of the deal, the X-Men franchise

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:26.419
may be to blame for Disney and Sony divorcing.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.560
"You picked the wrong house, bub."

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:33.219
The insider noted that Disney walked away
from negotiations partly because executives

00:00:33.219 --> 00:00:37.840
want Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige
to place his focus more on the Marvel properties

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.060
the studio recently acquired from Fox.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.760
Those properties include the X-Men, the Fantastic
Four, and many others.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.859
Shortly before Disney acquired most of Fox's
assets in March 2019, when the two companies

00:00:48.859 --> 00:00:53.800
merged under a $71.3 billion deal, it was
confirmed that Feige would be taking over

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.969
the X-Men movie franchise, and already had
ideas as to what he would do with the gang

00:00:57.969 --> 00:01:00.120
of mutants within the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.440
Namely, he wants to recast Wolverine with
a younger actor and evidently start things

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.700
over from square one.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.530
Longtime X-Men producer Lauren Shuler Donner,
who hired Feige as an associate producer on

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:16.210
2000's X-Men, stated to Deadline in February
2019 that Feige was, quote, "still dealing

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.720
with the wealth of characters and trying to
make sense of it all."

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:24.260
Feige's plan for the X-Men property reportedly
became much clearer in June 2019, following

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.860
the release of Dark Phoenix, the 12th entry
in the X-Men movie series.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:32.630
A financial and critical failure, Dark Phoenix
posted the lowest opening weekend of any X-Men

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.810
movie in history and is considered by some
to be the worst installment of the franchise

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:41.400
— which is disappointing given it was the
last-ever X-Men film produced by Fox.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:46.280
Reportedly, Dark Phoenix's box office bombing
spurred Disney brass to rework its priorities

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:50.540
at Marvel Studios, evidently wanting Feige
to focus on rebuilding the X-Men brand.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:55.880
A source close to Variety indicated that Walt
Disney Studios co-chairman Alan Bergman insisted

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.700
on an end to the Sony talks after Dark Phoenix
flopped.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:02.700
Though it's tempting to jump on the "X-Men
Killed Spider-Man" train, fans should take

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.439
this report with a grain of salt.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.900
No one but the parties involved in the Disney-Sony
split know what really happened, and plenty

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.460
of rumors have surfaced in the time since
the news broke.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.280
Some claim that Disney and Sony are secretly
working things out behind the scenes, while

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.440
others are convinced that what's done is done
and there's no turning back.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.270
At this point in time, it's anyone's guess
what's coming next — even with Feige and

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:26.470
Spider-Man actor Tom Holland having recently
addressed the situation.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:31.440
During the 2019 D23 Expo in late August, the
men spoke with Entertainment Weekly about

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.180
the studios' break-up and Spidey's MCU exit.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.500
Holland expressed gratitude for getting to
play Spider-Man for what he called five amazing

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.460
years with the character while Feige stated
that the deal between Disney and Sony was,

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:44.000
quote, "never meant to last forever."

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.840
"My parents… are dead."

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.380
It's interesting to consider Dark Phoenix
and the future of the X-Men franchise being

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:56.620
a major force behind Disney's decision to
walk away from the negotiating table and let

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.160
Sony regain sole ownership over Spider-Man.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.380
Holland's web-slinging hero has proven wildly
successful for both studios — with many

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.660
fans and critics agreeing that his iteration
of Spider-Man is the best one yet.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.230
The most recent franchise entry, Spider-Man:
Far From Home, earned over a billion dollars

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:15.020
worldwide to become Sony's top-earning movie
ever.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.320
One could argue that it makes little sense
that Disney and Marvel would prioritize fixing

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.390
a broken franchise over keeping a really good
thing going.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:26.840
Either way, if the studios really have split,
it's hard not to be worried about the fate

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.310
of that third Tom Holland-starring Spider-Man
movie.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.500
"Well at least we can all agree the third
one's always the worst."

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.920
However, it doesn't seem totally unreasonable
that Feige and company would want to end the

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.100
ongoing tug-of-war with Sony over Spider-Man
and instead focus their time and expertise

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.140
on building the X-Men film series back up.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.840
The Spider-Man movies clearly aren't hurting
for attention in any aspect, and, thanks to

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.680
Feige's input, are on the steadiest ground
they've been on since Sam Raimi's original

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:53.180
trilogy.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.540
It seems that the biggest takeaway from all
the Spidey-related news is this: Sony will

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.530
probably be fine, Disney and Marvel will probably
be fine, and both studios will hopefully be

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.120
able to co-exist in peace.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.000
Holland's Spider-Man isn't going anywhere
in the immediate future, and neither are fans

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.860
of the franchise… for now, at least.

